        "note": "The reference states that the reddish deposit was discovered in 1911 by Thomas Griffith Taylor at Taylor Glacier, Antarctica.",
        "correction": null
      },
      {
        "claim": "Early theories attributed the red color of Blood Falls to red algae, but testing revealed no algae was present.",
        "segment_index": 1,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "The text confirms early pioneers attributed the red color to red algae, but it was later proven to be due to iron oxides.",
